1
00:05:08,571 --> 00:05:14,571
She was having a perfectly bad day... Then he came along and spoiled it.

2
00:10:17,142 --> 00:10:23,142
One Fine Day is a romance, comedy film directed by Michael Hoffman.

3
00:15:25,714 --> 00:15:31,714
Melanie Parker, an architect and mother of Sammy, and Jack Taylor, a
newspaper columnist and father of Maggie, are both divorced.

4
00:20:34,285 --> 00:20:40,285
They meet one morning when overwhelmed Jack is left unexpectedly with
Maggie and forgets that Melanie was to take her to school.

5
00:25:42,857 --> 00:25:48,857
As a result, both children miss their school field
trip and are stuck with the parents.

6
00:30:51,428 --> 00:30:57,428
The two adults project their negative stereotypes of ex-spouses on each other, but end up
needing to rely on each other to watch the children as each must save his job.

7
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Humor is added by Sammy's propensity for lodging objects in
his nose and Maggie's tendency to wander.

8
00:41:08,571 --> 00:41:14,571
Melanie Parker, played by Michelle Pfeiffer.

9
00:46:17,142 --> 00:46:23,142
Jack Taylor, played by George Clooney.

10
00:51:25,714 --> 00:51:31,714
Maggie Taylor, Jack's daughter, played by Mae Whitman.

11
00:56:34,285 --> 00:56:40,285
Sammy Parker, Melanie's son, played by Alex D. Linz.

12
01:01:42,857 --> 01:01:48,857
Lew, Jack's boss, played by Charles Durning.

13
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
Mr. Yates, Jr., played by Jon Robin Baitz.

14
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
One Fine Day is a 1996 American romantic comedy-drama film directed by
Michael Hoffman, starring Michelle Pfeiffer and George Clooney.

15
01:17:08,571 --> 01:17:14,571
Linz and Mae Whitman play their children.

16
01:22:17,142 --> 01:22:23,142
The title comes from the 1963 song "One Fine Day" by
Carole King, which is heard in the film.

17
01:27:25,714 --> 01:27:31,714
Pfeiffer served as an executive producer for the film, which was
produced in association with her company Via Rosa Productions.

18
01:32:34,285 --> 01:32:40,285
The film was nominated for an Academy Award for Best
Original Song ("For the First Time").

19
01:37:42,857 --> 01:37:48,857
The film explores themes of single mother, divorced,
single father, family conflict, child custody.

20
01:42:51,428 --> 01:42:57,428
The tone is lighthearted and emotional.
